{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/","folio-assistant-core":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant-core/v0/ns/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-stack-like-structure","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:stack-like-structure","kind":"remark","title":"Stack-like structure of the direct limit algebra","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-jet-shell"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-direct-limit-algebra","cites":["references/yekutieli2008"],"tags":["stack","twisted-deformation","yekutieli"],"text":"stack-like-structure.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<a id=\"rem:stack-like-structure\"></a><p>The direct limit algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{A}_\\infty</code> (<a href=\"#def:direct-limit-algebra\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/direct-limit\">direct limit algebra</a>) is a global \"stack-like\" version of the local <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code> deformations. At each point <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">p \\in M</code>, the fibre algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathcal{O}_{q(p)}(\\mathrm{SU}(2))</code> defines a local twisted deformation <span class=\"cite\" data-keys=\"yekutieli2008\">[yekutieli2008]</span>. The direct limit assembles these into a global object on the jet shell <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">J^\\infty E</code> (<a href=\"#rem:jet-shell\" data-at=\"lifting-and-descent/direct-limit\">jet shell</a>).</p>\n","source":"folio/quantum-observable-universe/lifting-and-descent/stack-like-structure.md","heading":"Remark","number":"6.6.5","page":"b/rem-stack-like-structure","qa":{"counts":{"pass":62,"fail":0,"warn":0,"na":15,"unknown":0,"stale":0},"milnor":{"total":2,"notPassing":0}}}
